From 4ceb5e77d085b6ed2fed00c37ba26fb227dad77a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Marcelo Poblete (via Claude)" <marcelopoblete.us@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 22:05:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat: non-overlapping topology layout, zoom/pan/group-select,
 legend, wireless links

- Rework the topology diagram's default layout algorithm: switches and
  wireless radios each get a reserved horizontal column sized to how
  many cameras hang off them, laid out left-to-right, instead of
  dividing a fixed-width canvas evenly. This is what was causing icons
  to stack on top of each other once a project had more than a
  handful of switches/cameras.
- Cameras under each device are arranged in a small grid (up to 4 per
  row) instead of one crowded row.
- Add pan (drag background) and zoom (scroll wheel, +/- buttons,
  reset-view button) to the topology canvas, docked as a right-edge
  icon toolbar to match the map's controls.
- Add a group-select tool (drag a marquee box to select multiple
  nodes, then drag any of them to move the group together).
- Add an on-canvas legend explaining node icons (gateway/switch/
  wireless radio/camera), line styles (solid = wired, dashed orange =
  wireless), and status dot colors.
- Distinguish Wireless Radio devices and wireless-linked cameras with
  a distinct radio-wave icon, orange accent, and dashed connection
  lines, and surface a 'Wireless' badge in the detail panel.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
